Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.54,0:00:04.48,Italics,Raion,0,0,0,,What is all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.18,0:00:08.35,Italics,Raion,0,0,0,,What the hell... happened here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.54,0:00:26.46,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.77,0:01:44.92,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Welcome back, Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.92,0:01:46.65,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Did something happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.65,0:01:48.88,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I saw some craters on the asphalt out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.20,0:01:51.77,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I was just asking the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.77,0:01:53.44,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Go on, Kou.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.44,0:01:54.14,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.42,0:01:58.22,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Moments ago, I identified two intruders \Nentering the concealed area
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.22,0:02:00.60,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,as well as two escapees.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.05,0:02:04.71,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,One intruder and one escapee \Nhave been exterminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.30,0:02:09.19,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I terminated a man with scouting abilities
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.19,0:02:12.95,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,and Souma sacrificed himself \Nthrough large-scale materialization.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.95,0:02:17.91,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,However, I couldn't stop the other intruder \Nand Hikari Ebina's escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.91,0:02:18.95,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Did you trace them?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.26,0:02:22.34,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,The large-scale materialization gave \Nthem just enough time to get away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.34,0:02:23.91,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Their whereabouts are unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.91,0:02:25.42,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,It's my fault...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.42,0:02:27.36,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What's your fault?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.92,0:02:32.23,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I mean, none of this would have \Nhappened if it weren't for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.23,0:02:34.88,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I didn't even notice they planned this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.88,0:02:38.90,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,I wonder how they were able \Nto even locate us here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.87,0:02:40.90,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Raion.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.35,0:02:44.49,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,What did you tell Souma \Nwhen you brought him here?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.49,0:02:48.56,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I asked him to come with me to the power \Nstation since the power wasn't working.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.56,0:02:52.81,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,On the way over, I threatened him, \Ntelling him I was working with the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.81,0:02:56.04,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,I doubt anyone can resist \Nafter hearing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.04,0:03:00.58,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,And his absence could be easily explained \Nwith the guise of fixing the power.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.40,0:03:05.96,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}In that case, they likely haven't realized \Nthat Raion has changed sides.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.26,0:03:08.61,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,See! It's not your fault, Raion!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.61,0:03:10.04,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.45,0:03:14.69,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Queen has full trust \Nin Haruto's Negotiation Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.01,0:03:18.12,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Still, it's odd that the Materialization \NRight hasn't been released,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.12,0:03:20.97,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,even though its owner died.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.97,0:03:23.54,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Immobilization Right's principle fixation!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.54,0:03:26.94,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hirayama must have fixed \NSouma's Materialization Right!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.49,0:03:32.83,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The fixation will stand as long as Hirayama, \NKnight, and Lili don't all die.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.83,0:03:35.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}So that's why Yagihashi \Ndecided to save Lili.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.20,0:03:36.19,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Raion.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.53,0:03:40.35,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,That's enough for today. \NLet's regroup tomorrow night.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.35,0:03:42.24,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Sometimes the best thing is to wait and see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.24,0:03:43.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Sure, I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.24,0:03:43.74,Default-Top,Emperor,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.74,0:03:46.09,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,But he just got here! Right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.09,0:03:47.73,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Don't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.07,0:03:52.21,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,There's no need to fill us in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.77,0:03:55.71,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,People died again because of me...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.47,0:03:59.75,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Maybe I should just stop trying.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.09,0:04:05.36,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Hayato and Sensei gave their lives \Nbecause they believed in you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.36,0:04:09.40,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Stop whining and live up to their faith,\Nif you consider them your friend!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.40,0:04:11.74,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,I've already decided to give my all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.74,0:04:15.17,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Those two didn't fight \Nso we could mope around!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.71,0:04:17.88,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.30,0:04:20.47,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,You're right, I shouldn't be the one mourning.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.91,0:04:25.23,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Raion-kun, you've done \Nyour part to the fullest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.83,0:04:27.91,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Whether that'll bear fruit
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.91,0:04:30.48,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,will depend entirely \Non Ebina-kun's information.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.72,0:04:34.50,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,I'm here with information \Nfrom Hirayama and Iruga.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.11,0:04:37.26,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,First off is Seraphiel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.59,0:04:39.85,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,His full name is Gonzaburo Tanonaka.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.85,0:04:42.62,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,There's no doubt he's a genuine priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.62,0:04:44.72,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,Iruga checked at City Hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.72,0:04:46.05,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Seraphiel...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.05,0:04:48.06,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Gonzaburo Tanonaka...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.06,0:04:52.69,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,As for his Prime Right, all we know is \Nthat it's under the Production Attribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.69,0:04:55.42,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,And I'm not sure what this refers to, but,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.42,0:05:00.03,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,something is supposed to "ignite" \Nat 21:00 on the day after my escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.73,0:05:05.33,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,Finally, this is a message from Hirayama.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.78,0:05:11.00,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,"We've organized a plan to defeat \NQueen Kisaragi... to commence today."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.00,0:05:12.59,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Defeat the Queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.59,0:05:15.42,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Is that even possible, like for real?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.45,0:05:19.46,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,As long as he works together with Fukami.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.87,0:05:23.05,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,So, Hirayama and Fukami.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.38,0:05:25.85,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,What is all this fuss about?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.85,0:05:27.03,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Lady Kisaragi...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.03,0:05:30.18,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,This man, Yohei Fukami is a traitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.18,0:05:31.72,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.72,0:05:34.91,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Hikari Ebina's escape \Nwas organized by Fukami!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.69,0:05:38.63,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,There was something off about \Nthat woman from the start!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.63,0:05:41.70,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,That's why I befriended her and \Nkept her under my surveillance!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.03,0:05:44.59,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,I've seen him talking with her many times!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.59,0:05:46.91,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I was wondering what this was about.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.91,0:05:49.36,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,You better cut the crap!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.89,0:05:53.37,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like Fukami says, \Nhis accusation is quite a reach...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.72,0:05:57.09,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've kept Hirayama on a long leash figuring \Nhe'd expose himself eventually,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.56,0:06:00.80,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}but how unfortunate for Fukami \Nto be used like this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.19,0:06:05.26,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,The Queen has next to zero \Ntrust in Hirayama and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.26,0:06:10.48,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,We'll use that to build \Nher trust in Fukami instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.48,0:06:14.20,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Lady Kisaragi, you wouldn't mind \Nif I killed him, would ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.20,0:06:15.14,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I suppose not.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.14,0:06:17.73,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,If that's what you want, I won't hold back!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.73,0:06:20.97,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Prime Right of Immobilization! \NImmobilize his heart!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.63,0:06:23.45,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Wha—?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.92,0:06:25.99,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,My Immobilization Right isn't working?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.99,0:06:28.95,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I've engaged a counter attack \Nwith my Transfer Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.95,0:06:33.11,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,If you don't display an intent \Nto transfer your Prime Right to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.11,0:06:35.42,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,your attack will rebound back to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.89,0:06:39.13,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,You have a choice between \Nyour Prime Right and your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.13,0:06:42.01,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Transfer Right can do that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.01,0:06:47.28,Italics,Hikari,0,0,0,,We'll lie about the Transfer Right's \Nability so she'll look on as they fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.28,0:06:48.96,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Fine, take that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.70,0:06:50.47,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Transfer!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.60,0:06:56.04,Italics,Hikari,0,0,0,,We've confirmed that the Evasion Right \Ncan't stop the Transfer Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.67,0:06:59.06,Italics,Hikari,0,0,0,,So if we can blindside her, \Nthat should finish the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.42,0:07:01.07,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Hang on, Hikari.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.44,0:07:03.24,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Are you saying that...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.24,0:07:08.25,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Fukami killing Rika was part \Nof your plan all along?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.25,0:07:13.97,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,We needed to do whatever we could \Nto gain her trust and let her guard down.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.97,0:07:14.75,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.79,0:07:18.83,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,But it helped to create \Nan opening to the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.83,0:07:22.10,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,If we can just time it right, she won't \Nbe able to stop the Transfer Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.59,0:07:25.04,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,No, I don't think it'll be that easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.72,0:07:27.93,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You may be able to kill the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.93,0:07:31.19,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,However... your plan will fail.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.53,0:07:40.33,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,I expected this to happen anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.69,0:07:43.69,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,As long as the Queen's dead, \Nthat's all that matters!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.96,0:07:46.20,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I've finally settled things.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.20,0:07:49.49,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Fukami, ready for the final blow?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.49,0:07:50.95,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Let's do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.56,0:07:54.08,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,{\i1}I command Kou Kirishima's heart to...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.56,0:07:54.08,Default-Top,Fukami,0,0,0,,{\i1}Send my injuries to Kou...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.47,0:07:55.70,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,Immobilize!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.47,0:07:55.70,Default-Top,Fukami,0,0,0,,Transfer!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.49,0:07:57.84,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.84,0:08:00.88,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,We've prepared in case things came to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.60,0:08:06.51,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Prime Right of Resurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.18,0:08:18.93,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,How careless of me... \NI didn't see that coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.93,0:08:20.58,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Your clothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.58,0:08:22.67,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Allow me to change it back \Nwith the Recurrence Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.49,0:08:25.28,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,{\i1}That can't be...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.80,0:08:29.20,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,{\i1}So that's how!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.32,0:08:31.91,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,Fail?! What are you talking about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.91,0:08:33.54,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It's very simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.12,0:08:36.57,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Queen doesn't own the powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.57,0:08:38.87,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The owner is her deputy officer, Kou.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.14,0:08:42.76,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,How did I fail to notice...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.76,0:08:44.90,Default,Hirayama,0,0,0,,It was you all along... Kou...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.90,0:08:47.59,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,D-Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.43,0:08:52.30,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The time has come...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.74,0:08:56.77,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It's time to tell you all the truth, \Nnow that the stars have aligned.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.24,0:09:01.27,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Sudo-kun and I are working \Ntogether with Iruga-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.27,0:09:03.91,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We'll explain from the very beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.91,0:09:05.73,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Stay calm and listen carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.26,0:09:10.07,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Queen's ultimate goal \Nis to find Teppei Yoshii
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.36,0:09:12.41,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,and seize the Obedience Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.41,0:09:15.46,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Teppei Yoshii... Isn't he the guy who's...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.46,0:09:18.37,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Iruga's best friend and owner \Nof the Obedience Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.37,0:09:21.37,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,He's the one who died during the test run.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.37,0:09:23.04,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,One month ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.47,0:09:25.85,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,After we declared the end of Tasuketsu,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.85,0:09:28.74,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Ren Iruga returned to the Camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.30,0:09:32.53,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,There, he happened to see Maria Kisaragi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.99,0:09:35.97,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,This is before she first \Nappeared as the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.51,0:09:38.44,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Why would she go to the Camp?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.44,0:09:41.98,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,And how did she even know \Nabout it in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.98,0:09:47.90,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Apparently, the Queen was looking over some \Ndocuments about the Emperor and Teppei-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.90,0:09:51.58,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,That's how she found out about \NTeppei Yoshii's Obedience Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.58,0:09:54.24,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,But why was she researching those two?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.66,0:09:56.00,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's because...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.54,0:10:00.00,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,the three of them are blood siblings.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.01,0:10:01.97,Show Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(492,245)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.53,0:10:07.54,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,It wasn't just the Emperor and the Queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.54,0:10:10.12,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Teppei Yoshii was related too?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.42,0:10:12.88,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,As I explained before,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.88,0:10:15.25,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,they're relatives of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.25,0:10:17.92,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Not that we were ever very close.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.44,0:10:22.51,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,One day, their parents passed away \Nin a car accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.51,0:10:26.73,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The three of them were each \Nadopted by a different family.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.57,0:10:30.55,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The eldest daughter, Maria, \Nby the Kisaragis in Saitama,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.55,0:10:33.30,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,the first-born son, Teppei,\Nby the Yoshiis in Okayama,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.30,0:10:36.52,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,and the second-born son, Haruto, \Nby the Yanagis in Saitama.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.86,0:10:40.40,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,We were such distant relatives, \Nall the arrangements had been made
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.40,0:10:42.81,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,by the time we found out what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.41,0:10:47.29,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,No wonder they all have \Ndifferent last names.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.81,0:10:51.97,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Maria Kisaragi always had \Na strong love for her family,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.97,0:10:54.50,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,but I imagine it's only grown stronger \Nwith the death of her parents
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.50,0:10:57.51,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,and being separated from her siblings.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.88,0:11:00.05,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You see, she wants them all back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.05,0:11:03.79,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Her family... and everything she loves.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.62,0:11:08.78,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}That explains the Queen's full trust \Nin the Negotiation Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.78,0:11:11.73,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}As long as the Emperor says so, \Nshe believes it's foolproof.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.23,0:11:16.82,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}She won't second guess the Emperor \Nbecause she loves him as her little brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.25,0:11:21.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just like Kazuki always \Nbelieved in me, no matter what...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.82,0:11:27.38,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}That doesn't make any of what \Nthey did okay. But still...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.38,0:11:29.21,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,That Tasuketsu the other day...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.33,0:11:30.84,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,95)\an8}You're a male with the blood type RH-O
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.33,0:11:30.84,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,163)}who has lived in Niimi City, Okayama Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.04,0:11:35.59,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,The male with the blood type RH-O \Nwho lived in Niimi, Okayama...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.59,0:11:38.39,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,It was about Teppei Yoshii.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.73,0:11:45.14,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Hang on, that question was meant \Nto keep Teppei alive, which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.67,0:11:48.70,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Queen doesn't know that he's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.20,0:11:52.83,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,And as one of the casualties \Nfrom the test run,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.83,0:11:54.86,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Teppei Yoshii's body should be \Na part of the tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.86,0:11:58.61,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,What?! Is that how that tower \Nwas made, for real?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.03,0:12:01.83,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,If the Queen's side were ever \Nto figure that out,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.83,0:12:07.21,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,naturally, she'll turn the tower back \Ninto a pile of bodies and revive him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.21,0:12:11.17,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Resurrection Right was for \Nin case Teppei had died?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.57,0:12:16.09,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Her vision is to revive and reunite with her \Nsiblings in a church with the priest's blessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.09,0:12:20.08,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's why she selected their base as \Nthat church, together with Seraphiel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.08,0:12:23.15,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Blessing? What does that \Nhave to do with anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.15,0:12:24.94,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It means everything to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.94,0:12:26.98,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,She's reuniting with her siblings, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.40,0:12:32.19,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Everything clicked when I learned \Nthat Seraphiel is a real priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.19,0:12:34.86,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,So how do you know Kou owns the powers?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.86,0:12:36.63,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,There's no definitive proof.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.63,0:12:40.82,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,But based on the information we've \Ngathered, it's the only viable option.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.44,0:12:44.88,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We assumed so by the time \Nwe helped Knight escape,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.88,0:12:47.55,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,which is why we separated Kou from the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.55,0:12:51.71,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,As a result, the Queen couldn't stop \Nso much as the Suspension Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.14,0:12:55.60,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Of her first servants, the only one \Nwho's survived this entire time
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.60,0:12:58.08,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,is Kou of the Three Powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.54,0:13:01.74,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,It's not the Queen who holds the powers \Nwith Kou being the brains.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.74,0:13:05.78,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Rather, it's most likely the opposite.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.78,0:13:09.97,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Besides, the main culprit and \Nfundamental source is the itako
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.97,0:13:12.35,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,who brought the Rights into this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.35,0:13:13.98,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\an8\c&H515152&}Saneatsu Narita's Medical Records
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.13,0:13:14.44,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Camp already existed
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.00,0:13:16.23,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,One Kidney Lost in Accident
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.44,0:13:19.24,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,when Narita-kun was handed \Nthe Parental Authority eleven years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.57,0:13:21.91,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,At the time, Maria Kisaragi was just thirteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.25,0:13:24.16,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Emperor was only a baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.16,0:13:28.16,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Not to mention, their parents were \Nhealthy and she lived a normal life.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.16,0:13:31.52,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,In other words, it makes no sense \Nfor her to be the itako.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.52,0:13:34.08,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The itako is Kou of the Three Powers!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.08,0:13:37.05,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So what are we supposed to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.59,0:13:41.84,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Don't you see? We have \Ntwo ultimate trump cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.84,0:13:43.18,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Trump cards?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.18,0:13:47.13,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The first is Ren Iruga.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.13,0:13:51.94,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,He'll inform the Queen of Teppei Yoshii's \Ndeath and lead her to the final stage.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.53,0:13:54.23,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's the "ignition."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.75,0:13:56.38,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Since we've already gathered all the facts,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.38,0:14:00.14,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,we can predict the Queen's moves \Nand strategize for battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.14,0:14:01.72,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,What's the second one?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.19,0:14:04.01,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I suspect you already know.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.92,0:14:09.91,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Now allow me to share the details of our plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.49,0:14:15.04,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Remember your roles as I just explained.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.04,0:14:18.29,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Ignition is set for tomorrow at 21:00.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.29,0:14:19.88,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I'll be off now,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.88,0:14:21.47,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,to start "prepping."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.23,0:14:28.43,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've connected all the dots.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.00,0:14:34.47,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,{\i1}Iruga and Teppei both escaped during \Nthe Camp's major breach three years ago.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.43,0:14:38.81,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,{\i1}Teppei ran to Kanagawa in search \Nof independence, and Iruga eventually{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.81,0:14:42.65,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,{\i1}entered our school after being taken \Nin by Gunjosora Orphanage in Tokyo.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.12,0:14:47.16,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's where he met Yagihashi, who \Nhe'd heard about from Teppei.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.16,0:14:48.21,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,{\i1}And...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.84,0:14:52.54,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Iruga-kun had stolen one \Nenvelope from the Camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.54,0:14:57.75,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,He gave it to me knowing I was \NTeppei-kun's cousin, just in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.75,0:15:01.46,Flashback,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,What?! So you were working \Nwith Iruga before Tasuketsu?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.79,0:15:05.66,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,No, that wasn't until after \Nwe defeated the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.66,0:15:11.01,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,When I heard about the Emperor \Nfrom Mido, I thought of Haruto-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.01,0:15:15.91,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Given my knowledge that Teppei-kun \Nand Haruto-kun were siblings,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.91,0:15:19.88,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I figured Iruga-kun would eventually \Nvisit the Emperor's tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.88,0:15:22.65,Flashback,Raion,0,0,0,,To see the remains \Nof Teppei's little brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.00,0:15:27.30,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's where I spoke with Iruga-kun \Nand learned of Maria Kisaragi's actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.30,0:15:32.37,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That led me to form this final plan:\Nfor the Queen to revive Teppei-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.37,0:15:34.58,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Hence the ignition.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.58,0:15:36.43,Flashback,Raion,0,0,0,,What?! But...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.43,0:15:38.79,Flashback,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Isn't it risky to let them \Nresurrect him on the spot?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.79,0:15:40.51,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Like I mentioned,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.51,0:15:43.46,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,she's the type of person to go out of \Nher way to select a church as her base.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.46,0:15:46.13,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,She even has her priest \Nfriend accompany her.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.13,0:15:51.81,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Her attachment to family and \Nthe church are very much real.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.81,0:15:56.02,Flashback,Raion,0,0,0,,You mean she'll take him back \Nto the church to revive him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.02,0:15:59.35,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,As far as I know, that would be her instinct.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.87,0:16:01.73,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's why this plan will...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.32,0:16:07.95,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Iruga, what did you just say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.95,0:16:12.28,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Hmm? Honestly, I'm a bit surprised \Nto see you so surprised!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.28,0:16:14.81,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,To repeat what I said...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.81,0:16:18.75,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Could the person you're searching \Nfor be Teppei Yoshii by any chance?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.22,0:16:22.21,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,How do you know Teppei?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.52,0:16:27.67,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Well you see, Teppei-chan was \Nmy best friend back at the Camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.67,0:16:29.09,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Best friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.68,0:16:34.18,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,95)\an8}You're a male with the blood type RH-O
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.68,0:16:34.18,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,163)}who has lived in Niimi City, Okayama Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.68,0:16:34.18,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,That question from the other day \Nfit his description and...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.57,0:16:37.71,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,The Emperor looks a bit \Nlike Teppei-chan, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.79,0:16:40.85,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Then what was his personality like?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.18,0:16:44.03,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,He has a strong sense of justice, he's honest,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.03,0:16:46.96,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,but also kinda ditsy and a bit nosy!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.96,0:16:48.95,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,You really do know him...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.44,0:16:50.79,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Not only that,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.79,0:16:53.03,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,I know where Teppei-chan is.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.25,0:16:56.12,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I-Is that true, Iruga?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.12,0:17:00.33,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Of course it is. I would never lie \Nto my best friend's siblings!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.33,0:17:02.71,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Tell me! Where is he?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.71,0:17:06.42,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,That's for you to find out tomorrow \Nnight, when Raion-kun comes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.32,0:17:09.77,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Seeing as he's the Emperor's \Nbest friend and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.77,0:17:12.09,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Wouldn't you wanna share \Nthat precious moment?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.09,0:17:15.18,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Yeah! I wanna wait to find out with Raion!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.18,0:17:20.67,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,I'm best friends with Teppei-chan, who's \N siblings with the Queen and Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.67,0:17:23.17,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,And somehow, we were all \Nable to meet each other!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.17,0:17:26.15,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,It's gotta be either fate or a miracle!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.15,0:17:29.33,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,We even have this church \Nas the perfect venue!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.33,0:17:32.11,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,I bet Teppei-chan will be \Nglad to reunite here!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.82,0:17:37.11,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,You're right. We will reunite,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.11,0:17:39.98,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,here in this church, with His blessing!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.64,0:17:46.51,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,A blue sky... white clouds...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.88,0:17:47.78,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Boo!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.63,0:17:52.41,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Jeez Knight, don't scare me like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.41,0:17:54.29,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,I scared Raion!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.98,0:18:01.88,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,He has zero sense of urgency.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.88,0:18:04.34,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,This is our only chance to relax.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.11,0:18:13.12,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,To be honest, I didn't trust you... Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.51,0:18:14.85,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.85,0:18:17.22,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I don't deny that I was being suspicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.22,0:18:19.27,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,And I didn't want any information getting out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.27,0:18:21.62,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,You're a difficult dude to deal with.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.46,0:18:27.31,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Why do you think the Queen went \Nto the Camp in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.16,0:18:35.33,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Everything began with the itako \Nsealing the Rights into envelopes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.82,0:18:41.35,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That itako being Kou Kirishima. I suspect he \Nwas a key person in the Camp's establishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.35,0:18:44.57,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The chief culprit...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.57,0:18:50.17,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Queen visited the Camp \Nbecause she was tipped off by Kou.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.17,0:18:52.28,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's the most reasonable explanation.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.68,0:18:55.57,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The Emperor didn't seem to know about Kou.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.57,0:18:59.02,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I bet the Queen couldn't \Nbring herself to admit
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.02,0:19:01.78,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,she worked with one of the Camp's founders.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.20,0:19:06.21,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The ignition is happening tonight, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.21,0:19:10.17,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's right, and that's the sign \Nto commence our final plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.17,0:19:13.88,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Which is a ridiculous plan, by the way. \NYou guys are crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.18,0:19:17.09,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You think so? I think it's appropriate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.09,0:19:19.60,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,It's crazy, but awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.60,0:19:21.43,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So I'll risk my life for it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.43,0:19:24.68,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You and Gobo-kun are our key players.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.68,0:19:26.56,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,We're counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.56,0:19:29.58,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Yeah, let's make it happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.76,0:19:33.51,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,The Emperor is playing with Kai.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.51,0:19:36.49,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I'll engage my Prime Right of Isolation.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.67,0:19:40.41,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I've isolated this room \Nfrom the outside world.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.41,0:19:43.14,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,This blocks any exchanges between the two.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.14,0:19:48.75,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,Is this how you defended against Hirayama-kun \Nand Fukami-kun's attacks yesterday?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.17,0:19:51.90,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,Kisaragi-san, you died, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.90,0:19:53.91,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,What did it feel like?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.91,0:19:56.42,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I wish you wouldn't ask me \Nsuch a vulgar question.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.42,0:19:58.51,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I apologize for yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.92,0:20:03.06,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,My late response caused you pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.06,0:20:04.89,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Please, that was nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.89,0:20:07.48,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,We're indebted to your powers anyways.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.48,0:20:10.11,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,But regardless, who knew...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.11,0:20:17.11,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,The Queen as the brains with no powers \Nand Kou-kun as the true ruler.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.59,0:20:19.59,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,This set up worked surprisingly well!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.26,0:20:23.37,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,What's the status of\NHirayama and Fukami's Rights?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.37,0:20:24.65,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Still no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.65,0:20:28.08,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,All released Rights are supposed \Nto be returned, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.58,0:20:30.91,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,But they didn't come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.91,0:20:32.83,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,It has to be the Immobilization Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.83,0:20:35.67,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,It's still in place even after their deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.33,0:20:40.14,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Oh well. The Transfer Right is a big loss, \Nbut we'll have to make do.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.14,0:20:44.64,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,Why don't you have Kou-kun gift you \Na Prime Right as well, Kisaragi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.64,0:20:47.13,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,It's not like it would cost you any sacrifices.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.13,0:20:50.65,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I'm fine. I don't like \Ndoing things I'm not used to.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.85,0:20:55.06,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Besides, everything will be over soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.06,0:21:00.40,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,After Iruga tells me where Teppei \Nis tonight, we'll be reunited.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.40,0:21:01.82,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,My wish will come true.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.31,0:21:05.42,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,Is that so... what a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.42,0:21:09.04,Default,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,We can use the Rights however \Nwe wish as long as we have "it,"
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.95,0:21:13.64,Default-Top,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,Kou-kun's greatest invention of the century:
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.00,0:21:17.01,Default-Top,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,The ultra space-time construction \Ninterference device.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.01,0:21:20.01,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,Either Fate, or a Miracle
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.74,0:21:19.60,Default-Top,Seraphiel,0,0,0,,The Mother Light...
